# Build context for the root Dockerfile.
#
# The two entries that actually matter are node_modules and dist:
#
#   * node_modules/ contains native binaries built for the host's platform and
#     libc (@tailwindcss/oxide ships prebuilt platform packages). Copying a
#     host-built tree into a linux/amd64 image produces failures that look
#     nothing like their cause, so stage 1 always runs its own `npm ci`.
#   * dist/ would let a stale local bundle shadow what stage 1 just built.
#
# Everything else here is size and hygiene.

# Version control and CI.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Dependencies and build output — rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.nodeenv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local Python environments. A broken virtualenv (.local/) was committed to this
# repository once; it must never reach a build context either.
.local
.venv
venv
env
ENV

# Build-worker state and logs.
**/.frontend_build_status.json
**/.frontend_build.lock
**/.frontend_build.log
**/*.log

# Secrets and local environment files. `.env.example` is documentation and is
# deliberately kept so the image can be inspected for what it expects.
.env
**/.env
.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.flask_secret_key
**/.flask_secret_key.tmp.*
*.pem
*.key
*.token

# Not needed to build or run the image. Root-level names are listed explicitly
# alongside the **/ forms rather than relying on **/ matching zero directories.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
render.yaml
**/render.yaml
railway.json
**/railway.json
railway.toml
**/railway.toml
README.md
**/README.md
tests
**/tests
coverage
**/coverage
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode
.idea
**/*.swp
